        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Three Indian crew missing as US says fired on tanker off Oman Middle East Issued on: 10/06/2026 - 20:25 Three Indian crew members were reported missing after a vessel was attacked off Oman, India said Wednesday, before the US military announced it had fired on a tanker attempting to breach its blockade of Iran. In a statement, the Indian foreign ministry condemned the attack on the vessel, the Settebello, saying: \"Of the 24 Indian crew onboard, 21 Indians have been rescued thus far and three Indians are reportedly missing\". FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani has more. Israeli airstrikes kill 13 in south Lebanon, Lebanese sources say 10/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran deal 'wouldn't resolve anything': Trump trapped between 'unwinnable war, unpresentable deal' 10/06/2026 Middle East Trump vows response after Iran shoots down US helicopter 09/06/2026 Middle East Lebanon says 8 dead in strike on Tyre as Israel keeps up attacks on south 09/06/2026 Middle East France bans Israeli minister Smotrich in coordinated sanctions push 09/06/2026 Middle East Israel continues strikes on Beirut suburb 09/06/2026 Middle East Trump remains optimistic peace deal can be reached despite Middle East flare-up 09/06/2026 Middle East In Beirut's Hezbollah-controlled suburbs, war with Israel comes at a price for residents 09/06/2026 Middle East Netanyahu comes out of Iran flare-up a 'humiliated, failed war leader' 09/06/2026 Middle East"
